155
00:26:00.110 --> 00:26:16.699
Hart Montgomery: the scenario where someone incubates a standard in LFDT, or the Linux Foundation, and then moves it later to a more formal standards body once it's been baked in. This is a very common use of LF standards these days.

156
00:26:16.790 --> 00:26:35.569
Hart Montgomery: We think this is critical in very fast-moving areas, many of which LFDT operates in, because the traditional standards orgs don't necessarily allow you to move quickly enough. They're slow and deliberate, which is great for some things.

157
00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:43.709
Hart Montgomery: But if you're in an area where the technology is moving really fast, and you need to have something, we need something a little faster.

158
00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:54.790
