159
00:26:55.110 --> 00:26:57.950
Hart Montgomery: I think you all understand this already.

160
00:26:58.060 --> 00:27:02.490
Hart Montgomery: So I'm not going to go… Too deep into this.

161
00:27:04.080 --> 00:27:16.110
Hart Montgomery: I think the key point is we need resilience and portability, even in rapidly evolving technical school landscapes. Things like digital identity, tokenization.

162
00:27:16.670 --> 00:27:30.889
Hart Montgomery: all of these things are changing extremely quickly. Digital identity is a specially interesting case, because the technology, used, which is typically zero-knowledge proof-based, is changing extremely quickly.

163
00:27:31.240 --> 00:27:43.470
Hart Montgomery: And it's very, very hard to keep up with that with a traditional standards org. A lot… by the time the technology is already standardized, it's already out of date.

164
00:27:45.150 --> 00:27:50.189
Hart Montgomery: So… This is important, you know, particularly in this context.

165
00:27:52.850 --> 00:27:54.840
Hart Montgomery: So again,

166
00:27:55.120 --> 00:28:12.530
